          </fr:frontmatter>
          <fr:mainmatter>
            <html:p>
    How a proof about a long computation is assembled from proofs about short ones. Every zkVM that proves a real workload is doing this, and it is where the soundness argument becomes hardest to keep track of — the <fr:link href="/dhsorens-003M/" title="Nova and Folding Schemes" uri="https://derekhsorensen.com/dhsorens-003M/" display-uri="dhsorens-003M" type="local">Nova bug</fr:link> is the standing example.
</html:p>
