              <fr:mainmatter>
                <html:p>
    The folding design space after Nova: which constraint systems can be folded, how many instances at once, and what the recursive circuit costs.
</html:p>
                <html:p>
    Questions this page should answer:
    <html:ul><html:li>HyperNova: folding <fr:link href="/dhsorens-002V/" title="CCS and the Unified View" uri="https://derekhsorensen.com/dhsorens-002V/" display-uri="dhsorens-002V" type="local">CCS</fr:link>, with per-step cost dominated by one MSM.</html:li>
        <html:li>ProtoStar: folding arbitrary low-degree polynomial maps, and what that generality buys.</html:li>
        <html:li>ProtoGalaxy and multi-instance folding; KiloNova and non-uniform PCD.</html:li>
        <html:li>The axes to compare on: constraint system, instances per fold, recursive circuit size, assumptions.</html:li>
        <html:li>Which of these is the right target for a formalisation, given that the definitions are still moving.</html:li></html:ul></html:p>
