          </fr:frontmatter>
          <fr:mainmatter>
            <html:p>
    Three group elements, a circuit-specific trusted setup, and a verifier cheap enough for the EVM. Obsolete as a zkVM backend and unavoidable as a <fr:link href="/dhsorens-003P/" title="Wrapping and On-Chain Verification" uri="https://derekhsorensen.com/dhsorens-003P/" display-uri="dhsorens-003P" type="local">wrapper</fr:link>.
</html:p>
            <html:p>
    Questions this page should answer:
    <html:ul><html:li>QAPs: from <fr:link href="/dhsorens-002S/" title="R1CS" uri="https://derekhsorensen.com/dhsorens-002S/" display-uri="dhsorens-002S" type="local">R1CS</fr:link> to a divisibility claim.</html:li>
        <html:li>The proof and the verification equation; why it is exactly three elements.</html:li>
        <html:li>The security argument in the algebraic group model, and what AGM assumes about the adversary. ArkLib has an <html:code>AGM</html:code> directory for this.</html:li>
        <html:li>Circuit-specific setup as the practical objection, and what universal setup changed.</html:li></html:ul></html:p>
